{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile (config_045, 0.725 acc) as the best configuration found. The only major untested variable across the top-performing family is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 has never been tested. config_006 pairs pca_n2000 with all other settings at their empirically best values (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile), directly testing whether a simpler linear encoder could match or exceed scvi_n200. While I expect scvi_n200 to remain superior (scgpt, a more complex learned model, already underperformed it), this is the highest-value remaining exploration because it is the only untested axis that could plausibly shift accuracy in either direction. As the final experiment, it either reveals a surprise gain or definitively confirms config_045 as the optimum. Expected cost: ~3.0–3.5 GPU hours (PCA encoding is cheaper than scVI, while the ViT-L image encoder and transformer aggregation dominate runtime), making it a modest addition to the 38.09 GPU hours already spent."
}

